{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Duplicate of cded-334b-a742-4082 (closed): the same two facade tests, failing with the same 'I/O operation on closed file' raised from logging emit. Root cause was already diagnosed there - install_stderr_handler (src/rebar/_logging.py) binds a StreamHandler to sys.stderr once and is idempotent by marker, so when an earlier in-process main() installs it while sys.stderr is a pytest capture stream, the handler keeps writing to that stream after it closes. Fix landed via Gerrit 3309; sibling duplicate 4c58-45d4-aaf7-48dc was closed against the same cause.\n\nFiled in error from a checkout pinned 260 commits behind at 2e28d817a7e. Re-checked against current origin/main (38c42c7e70e), where the fix is present. No separate work remains."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793844408416494001,"uuid":"7ba81321-098d-4853-9fb2-2964296f7a12"}